======================================================================
  OVERALL FINDINGS TABLE
======================================================================
  saved table: Table_FINDINGS_overall_v9.csv
  - H1 robustness (alt-IV/splits/FE/winsor): Negative across nearly all specs; β stable -0.0273 to -0.0152 under winsorisation.
      => H1 is not a specification artifact; weak spots are pre-COVID & US-only (disclosed).
  - Fama-MacBeth (H1): Time-series mean of yearly betas confirms the pooled estimate.
      => Result not driven by a single year or clustered-SE assumption.
  - Distress threshold sensitivity: Significant at 1/2/3pp thresholds; null at 5pp.
      => 5pp null is a POWER limit (few firms fall that far), not a failure.
  - IFRS/GAAP split (R6): H1 stronger in IFRS/non-US firms than US-GAAP firms.
      => Not a US-GAAP/LIFO accounting artifact; international firms carry H1.
  - Placebo battery (R7): Reverse-time p=0.14; permuted p=0.53 (both null); real p=0.014.
      => Real effect survives falsification; not spurious panel structure.
  - OLD-H4 semiconductor rejection: Semis NOT significant under 13 distinct specifications (alt-IV, alt-ref, US/intl, FM, subperiod).
      => The v8 sector centrepiece is comprehensively rejected — not a single-spec result.

